{
  "//": [
    "Every Test262 feature token this census has seen, and what the ledger says about it.",
    "",
    "FOUR CLASSES, and the distinction is the point:",
    "  inapplicable  a typescript.md \u00a713 non-goal. Refused on principle, never to be fixed,",
    "                and must not sit in a backlog. Carries a reason and the authority.",
    "  gap           a \u2717 or \u25d0 row. This is the backlog.",
    "  supported     a \u2705 row. The census expects these files to lower.",
    "  host          needs a host capability (realms, agents, detached buffers).",
    "",
    "THIS NEVER FILTERS. Every selected file is compiled whatever its features say, and",
    "the class is a column on the row. That is the only arrangement in which a wrong",
    "classification is detectable, and it is detectable in BOTH directions:",
    "  a file classed `inapplicable` that LOWERS   -> the classification is wrong",
    "  a file classed `supported` that ALL REFUSE  -> the ledger row is wrong",
    "The second is not hypothetical: typescript.md's `namespace` row was \u2705 and false,",
    "probed 2026-09-14, and `x!` and decorators are \u2717 rows that silently produce wrong",
    "answers rather than refusing.",
    "",
    "UNCERTAIN TOKENS ARE `gap`, deliberately. A gap that turns out to be supported sits",
    "in a backlog and is corrected by the audit; a non-goal that is really a gap",
    "disappears. The safe direction is the one that stays visible.",
    "",
    "Names are test262's own, from third_party/test262/features.txt at the pin.",
    "tooling/census/audit.mjs checks that every name here still exists there, which is",
    "how an upstream rename is caught rather than silently reclassified."
  ],
